body:
**Bevy version**

"0.4.0" - Crates.io

**Operating system & version**

Windows 10 -19042.782

**What you did**

If you draw images next to each-other with Bevy, it seems that if the window size is odd, they are not placed as expected. As an example, I created an image that is 10 x 10 pixels. I then set them next to each-other.

<details>
<summary>See Code</summary>

```
use bevy::{prelude::*, transform};

fn main() {
    App::build()
        .add_resource(ClearColor(Color::BLACK))
        .add_resource(WindowDescriptor{
            width: 799.0,
            height: 600.0,
            title: String::from("Draw"),
            ..Default::default()
        })
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_startup_system(setup.system())
        .run();
}

fn draw_thing(commands: &mut Commands, asset_server: &Res<AssetServer>,texture_atlases: &mut ResMut<Assets<TextureAtlas>>,pos_x: f32, pos_y: f32,index: u32) -> Option<Entity> {
    let texture_handle = asset_server.load("images/draw.png");
    let texture_atlas = TextureAtlas::from_grid(texture_handle,Vec2::new(10.0,10.0),10,1);
    let texture_atlas_handle = texture_atlases.add(texture_atlas);
    Some(commands
        .spawn(SpriteSheetBundle{
            texture_atlas: texture_atlas_handle,
            sprite: TextureAtlasSprite {
                color: Color::WHITE,
                index: index,
            },
            transform: Transform {
                translation: Vec3::new(pos_x,pos_y,0.0),
                ..Default::default()
            },
            ..Default::default()
        }).current_entity().unwrap())
}

fn setup(
    commands: &mut Commands,
    asset_server: Res<AssetServer>,
    mut texture_atlases: ResMut<Assets<TextureAtlas>>,
) {
    commands.spawn(Camera2dBundle::default());
    for i in 1..20 {
        draw_thing(commands,&asset_server,&mut texture_atlases,i as f32 *10 as f32,0.0, 0);
    }
}
```


</details>

**What you expected to happen**

I expect that the images will be lined up perfectly next to each other despite window size.

**What actually happened**

What happens is depending on the size of the window, the display is different.
